## Required CAS preservation and obsolete stock handle

The following historical exact CAS assertions must remain in the candidate
universe with their original whole-row holds. After verifying actual presence,
the installation action is **INSTALL_WITHHOLD**, never automatic support:

| Stable subject | Predicate | CAS |
| --- | --- | --- |
| MIM:0000146 | skos:exactMatch | cas:14919-49-4 |
| MIM:0000327 | skos:exactMatch | cas:12054-85-2 |
| MIM:0000349 | skos:exactMatch | cas:55449-49-5 |
| MIM:0000365 | skos:exactMatch | cas:65710-07-8 |

Inspect the actual preserved complete rows, source/comment vocabulary and old
reasons. Form-specific core identity does not clear unresolved synonyms,
product scope or prior negative evidence. A missing CAS row is a stop for
generator/preservation reconciliation, not a REMOVE_WITH_HISTORY rationale.
Preserve old reasons as historical observations. If a prior reason describes
chemistry already corrected in the current owner, state that distinction rather
than repeating the stale contradiction as a current fact; the unclosed
whole-row hold still does not silently become support.
For ammonium heptamolybdate, retain the known ChEBI prose error as a limitation:
its tetrahydrate label/formula is not evidence for the conflicting seven-water
wording. Do not use the earlier failed supplier fetches as positive evidence.

Separately review any derived removal of
`MIM:0002332 skos:exactMatch kgmicrobe.compound:sodium_nitrate_070_m_stock`.
The exact original row, current stock owner, closed #684 history and current
diagnostic proposal establish the bounded question. The actual current
`kgmicrobe.ingredient:sodium_nitrate_~28070_m_stock~29` identity and
`skos:broadMatch CHEBI:63005` relation must survive distinctly. Removal is only
`REMOVE_WITH_HISTORY` after genuine current paired assessment of the actual
selection, with all old cells/tokens/stamps/reasons retained. Neither survivor
inherits support: their existing whole-row holds remain until independently
resolved. No replacement handle is invented from a filename or parent prefix.

## Historical and suppression obligations

Every native history target must be assessed with
`PRESERVE_HISTORICAL_OBLIGATIONS`, including the exact W01 thirteen-comment and
W09 eight-row primary/skeptical lineages. Preserve their scopes, negative evidence,
old timestamps and source pins; comment retention is not release support. Keep
the original campaign case/origin accounting and all source-binding holds.

The complete native suppression object gets its own
`PRESERVE_SUPPRESSION_HISTORY` assessment: prior and generated vocabularies,
merged evidence, retired-subject history and actual `other` token exclusions.
Do not resurrect rejected acid/anion names, withdrawn PC structural aliases or
old owner collisions. Preserved comments may state historical values; they must
not silently become current identity authority.

## Native report and downstream boundaries

Follow `AUTHORING-SCAFFOLD.md`. Both primary and a separate independent skeptic
must assess every actual selection row/removal plus every native history target
and the suppression object. An installation assessment's `outcome: supported`
for `INSTALL_WITHHOLD` supports safe preservation under a hold; it is not positive
chemical support. Any unresolved applicable installation finding must be
resolved through its real issue/curation path, not hidden in a passing report.

After paired scientific reports, the native prepared publication set still needs
a separate independent technical acceptance. Canonical installation is not
ordinary reviewed SSSOM release, companion KGX acceptance or reviewed source-to-MIM
identity export. Those later products require their own actual current inputs,
complete supported/withheld accounting and validation. No KG rebuild or merge.
